course: dictionary
lesson: 10498
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is meant. The short word TV is a good example. «Everett's dad yells at the TV» tells you TV is the machine with a screen, because you can yell at a machine but you watch its pictures.
explain: «The whole family watches the TV Gala together» on New Year's Eve. Here TV means the programmes that are shown. Ask yourself: is this a thing, a show, or a job? The words around the word give the answer.
explain: «She works in TV» means she works in the business of making programmes. Check by swapping in your meaning: she works in television-making, which still makes sense. TV is short for television, and telly is another word for it in the UK.
fact: TV means television, a machine with a screen that shows programmes, films and news.
fact: TV can also mean the programmes that are shown, as in watching TV, or the business of making them, as in working in TV.
fact: Useful phrases include «TV show», «TV channel», «on TV» and «turn on the TV».
fact: Safety rule: big TVs can tip over, so never climb on furniture to reach one, and TVs should be fixed to the wall.
fact: In science, a TV screen makes its pictures from tiny dots of light called pixels.
exercise: «Everett's dad yells at the TV.» What is the TV in this sentence? | *A machine with a screen | A family dinner | A tree in the garden | The business of making programmes
exercise: «The whole family watches the TV Gala together.» What does TV mean here? | A kind of phone | A park with swings | A machine that makes dumplings | *The programmes that are shown
exercise: «She works in TV.» What does TV mean here? | A remote control | *The business of making programmes | A sports team | A channel on the radio
test: «Please turn off the TV, it is time for bed.» What does TV mean here? | *A machine with a screen | A show about sport | A tv-shaped cake | A kind of lamp
test: Which word is another name for TV used in the UK? | Telephone | Radio | Computer | *Telly
exam: Maya reads «Most TV romances end after the show.» What does TV mean here? | *The programmes that are shown | A type of mobile phone | A machine on a wall | Television in the sense of the business of making shows
